retention in ",[202,203,204],"strong",{},"Wolf Settings → Retention",".",[207,208,210],"h2",{"id":209},"resolutions","Resolutions",[212,213,214,233],"table",{},[215,216,217],"thead",{},[218,219,220,224,227,230],"tr",{},[221,222,223],"th",{},"Resolution",[221,225,226],{},"DocType",[221,228,229],{},"Default retention",[221,231,232],{},"Read by",[234,235,236,251,270],"tbody",{},[218,237,238,242,245,248],{},[239,240,241],"td",{},"Raw samples",[239,243,244],{},"Wolf Metric Sample",[239,246,247],{},"48 hours",[239,249,250],{},"Rule windows up to 3 h, the 1 h chart",[218,252,253,256,264,267],{},[239,254,255],{},"1-minute rollups",[239,257,258,259,263],{},"Wolf Metric Rollup (",[260,261,262],"code",{},"resolution"," 60)",[239,265,266],{},"30 days",[239,268,269],{},"Windows up to 2 days (6 h and 24 h charts)",[218,271,272,275,280,283],{},[239,273,274],{},"1-hour rollups",[239,276,258,277,279],{},[260,278,262],{}," 3600)",[239,281,282],{},"365 days",[239,284,285],{},"Longer windows (7 d chart)",[198,287,288],{},"A rollup row stores, for one series (metric, host, bench, site, labels) in one bucket:",[290,291,292,296,299,302,305],"ul",{},[293,294,295],"li",{},"count;",[293,297,298],{},"sum;",[293,300,301],{},"min;",[293,303,304],{},"max;",[293,306,307],{},"the last value, with its time.",[198,309,310,311,314,315,314,318,314,321,314,324,327,328,331],{},"So ",[260,312,313],{},"avg",", ",[260,316,317],{},"min",[260,319,320],{},"max",[260,322,323],{},"sum",[260,325,326],{},"count"," and ",[260,329,330],{},"last"," over whole buckets equal the raw answer.",[198,333,334],{},"A read takes, in order:",[336,337,338,341,344],"ol",{},[293,339,340],{},"the coarsest resolution allowed for its window, up to the last rolled bucket;",[293,342,343],{},"then finer rollups;",[293,345,346],{},"then the raw samples not rolled up yet, so the newest minutes are always there.",[198,348,349],{},"A long window loses at most one bucket at its start: under a minute for 1-minute reads, under an\nhour for 1-hour reads.",[207,351,353],{"id":352},"rollups","Rollups",[198,355,356,357,360],{},"The ",[260,358,359],{},"rollup_metrics"," job runs every minute.",[290,362,363,366,372,375],{},[293,364,365],{},"It rolls closed minutes, 2 minutes after they end, and closed hours.",[293,367,368,369,205],{},"Its progress is in ",[202,370,371],{},"Wolf Rollup State",[293,373,374],{},"It recomputes whole buckets, so running it again never double counts.",[293,376,377],{},"Samples that arrive late, for example an agent replaying its spool, move the progress back.\nTheir buckets are rolled again, up to the raw retention.",[379,380,381],"tip",{},[198,382,383,384,387,388,392],{},"Rollups, like alert rules, depend on the scheduler tick. Set ",[260,385,386],{},"scheduler_tick_interval"," to 60 (see\n",[389,390,391],"a",{"href":31},"Install the Wolf App",").",[207,394,396],{"id":395},"purge","Purge",[198,398,399,402],{},[260,400,401],{},"purge_metrics"," runs hourly and applies the retention.",[404,405,406],"note",{},[198,407,408],{},"It never deletes raw samples or 1-minute rollups that are not rolled up yet.",[198,410,411,412,415],{},"Event retention (",[260,413,414],{},"event_retention_days",") is separate and unchanged by metric retention.",[207,417,419],{"id":418},"ingest-mode","Ingest mode",[198,421,422,423,205],{},"Set in ",[202,424,425],{},"Wolf Settings → Agents → Ingest Mode",[212,427,428,438],{},[215,429,430],{},[218,431,432,435],{},[221,433,434],{},"Mode",[221,436,437],{},"Behaviour",[234,439,440,455],{},[218,441,442,448],{},[239,443,444,447],{},[260,445,446],{},"async"," (default)",[239,449,450,451,454],{},"Validates a push, queues the inserts on the ",[260,452,453],{},"short"," queue and answers at once. A worker inserts the batch and attaches its events to open incidents. If the queue is unreachable, the push is stored inline.",[218,456,457,462],{},[239,458,459],{},[260,460,461],{},"sync",[239,463,464],{},"Stores during the request.",[198,466,467,468,205],{},"In both modes, the agent's last seen time, clock skew and Wolf's health are updated during the\nrequest. The answer an agent gets in each mode is in the\n",[389,469,471],{"href":470},"\u002Freference\u002Fprotocol#ingest-mode","protocol",[207,473,183],{"id":474},"performance",[198,476,477,478,205],{},"Metric rows are stored in metric and time order, and reads of known metrics scan the primary key\nby name range. Measured results at 100 hosts × 7 days are in\n",[389,479,183],{"href":184},[207,481,483],{"id":482},"optional-time-series-backend","Optional time-series backend",[485,486,487],"warning",{},[198,488,489,490,205],{},"Design only, ",[202,491,492],{},"not built",[198,494,495],{},"The read path goes through two functions:",[290,497,498,504],{},[293,499,500,503],{},[260,501,502],{},"rollups.aggregate()",", for rules;",[293,505,506,509],{},[260,507,508],{},"rollups.series_rows()",", for charts.",[198,511,512,513,205],{},"Writes go through ",[260,514,515],{},"events.insert_metrics()",[198,517,518],{},"A ClickHouse or TimescaleDB backend would implement those three:",[212,520,521,534],{},[215,522,523],{},[218,524,525,528,531],{},[221,526,527],{},"Part",[221,529,530],{},"ClickHouse",[221,532,533],{},"TimescaleDB",[234,535,536,550,572],{},[218,537,538,540,547],{},[239,539,241],{},[239,541,542,543,546],{},"A ",[260,544,545],{},"MergeTree"," table",[239,548,549],{},"A hypertable",[218,551,552,555,566],{},[239,553,554],{},"Minute and hour rollups",[239,556,557,558,561,562,565],{},"Materialized views (",[260,559,560],{},"AggregatingMergeTree"," with ",[260,563,564],{},"sumState\u002FminState\u002FmaxState\u002FargMaxState",")",[239,567,568,569],{},"Continuous aggregates with ",[260,570,571],{},"first\u002Flast",[218,573,574,577,580],{},[239,575,576],{},"Retention",[239,578,579],{},"TTL",[239,581,582],{},[260,583,584],{},"add_retention_policy",[198,586,587],{},"The watermark logic and the purge job would then be the database's job. Until a site needs more\nthan a few hundred hosts, the Frappe tables above are enough and keep Wolf a plain Frappe app.",{"title":589,"searchDepth":590,"depth":591,"links":592},"",1,2,[593,594,595,596,597,598],{"id":209,"depth":591,"text":210},{"id":352,"depth":591,"text":353},{"id":395,"depth":591,"text":396},{"id":418,"depth":591,"text":419},{"id":474,"depth":591,"text":183},{"id":482,"depth":591,"text":483},"How Wolf stores metrics at three resolutions, rolls them up, purges them and ingests pushes.","md",null,{},{"icon":181},{"title":178,"description":599},"9Mq_MGSo0IRLBz8NdrT7JJWehkdkyYBtmumMosRQQuk",[607,609],{"title":173,"path":174,"stem":175,"description":608,"icon":176},"The read and action APIs behind the Wolf UI at \u002Fwolf, their arguments, answers and access rules.",{"title":183,"path":184,"stem":185,"description":610,"icon":186},"Load test results at 100 hosts for 7 days, what changed to reach them, and how to run the test again.",1794994139024]